{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For the nakedness of the land you have come to see.</b> Rashi explained: for you entered through ten gates of the city. And if you ask, how did he know? Rather, in the Tanhuma it is explained: three decrees Joseph decreed — one, that no slave may enter Egypt to buy grain; and one, that a single person may not go after two donkeys; and one, that no person may enter until he writes his name and his father's name and his grandfather's name. What did Joseph do? He commanded that the names of the people who were registered day by day be brought to him. When Joseph's brothers came down, they entered ten through ten gates, just as their father had commanded them — 'why should you be seen?' The gatekeeper would say to them: what is your name? And he would answer: Reuben son of Jacob son of Isaac, and so all of them. The gatekeepers brought the lists to Joseph; once he read them, he knew they were his brothers."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:25.190192786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}